<%- cpus = user_context["cpu"].to_s.strip -%>
<%- mem  = user_context["memory"].to_s.strip -%>
<%- unless cpus.empty? || mem.empty? -%>
**Resources:** <%= cpus %> CPU<%= "s" unless cpus == "1" %>, <%= mem %> GB
<%- end -%>

Your desktop settings live in `~/cirrus-desktop/`, not in `~/.config` — so this
session cannot change how XFCE, GTK or Thunar behave anywhere else you log in.
Anything you want to keep, save it under your home directory as usual.

The session ends itself after an hour with nothing connected, so closing the tab
releases the CPU and memory rather than holding them.
